From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: apple: add keep_in_sleep for a sleep that
 arms the watchdog itself

The driver stops the watchdog at device suspend and starts it again at
device resume. A bring-up suspend-to-RAM sequence that arms it itself
for the whole sleep (apple-s2r with wdt_from_enter) then has a stretch
in device suspend, after this driver's callback, where nothing can
reset a hung machine.

Add keep_in_sleep, off by default: when set, the suspend and resume
callbacks leave the watchdog as it is.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/watchdog/apple_wdt.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/apple_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/apple_wdt.c
index 3c867a3ce6..1ec8eb3ac9 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/apple_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/apple_wdt.c
@@ -211,10 +211,21 @@ static int apple_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &wdt->wdd);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Bring-up: a suspend-to-RAM sequence that arms this watchdog itself for the
+ * whole sleep (apple-s2r's wdt_from_enter) needs it left running from the
+ * echo on, not stopped at device suspend and started again at device resume.
+ */
+static bool keep_in_sleep;
+module_param(keep_in_sleep, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(keep_in_sleep, "Bring-up: leave the watchdog as it is across system sleep, for a caller that arms it for the sleep itself (default: off)");
+
 static int apple_wdt_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_wdt *wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(keep_in_sleep))
+		return 0;
 	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd) || watchdog_hw_running(&wdt->wdd))
 		apple_wdt_start(&wdt->wdd);
 
@@ -225,6 +236,8 @@ static int apple_wdt_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_wdt *wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(keep_in_sleep))
+		return 0;
 	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd) || watchdog_hw_running(&wdt->wdd))
 		apple_wdt_stop(&wdt->wdd);
 
